        "original_id": "68bf6527-953d-56b5-a0ed-87064b40bc1c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Angostura bitters, Springbokkie\n- Companies: House of Angostura\n- Places: Trinidad and Tobago, South Africa\n- Concepts: bitters, botanically infused alcoholic mixtures, cocktail shooters, Afrikaans language\n\nFacts:\n- Angostura bitters is a concentrated bitters and a botanically infused alcoholic mixture made by House of Angostura in Trinidad and Tobago.\n- Angostura bitters is made of water, 44.7% ethanol, gentian, herbs, and spices.\n- The Springbokkie means \"little Springbok\" in the Afrikaans language.\n- The Springbokkie is a cocktail shooter composed of creme de menthe or substitutes and Amarula.\n- The Springbokkie is popular in South Africa.",
